--
--   Description
----------------------
-- This test checks the handling of frames with code/symbol errors by
-- the receive path.
--
-- 
-- Functional Coverage
----------------------
-- * Checks that gem_rx can detect rx_er active during any part of frame,
--   which are greater than MinFrameSize.
--   NOTE: short frames with code errors are already checked by rx_short* tests.
--
--  
-- Detailed Test Description
----------------------------
-- 1. Setup DMA wait states for the test.
-- 2. Initialise the GEM for 100Mbits/s 32-bit DMA mode.
-- 3. Enable all interrupts, and then enable receive.
-- 4. Receive a 64 byte frame with good CRC that has a symbol error on 
--    third nibble of preamble.
--    Ensure that the frame is discarded with a symbol error status.
-- 5. Receive a 64 byte frame with good CRC that has a symbol error on 
--    fourth nibble of preamble.
--    Ensure that the frame is discarded with a symbol error status.
-- 6. Receive a 64 byte frame with good CRC that has a symbol error on 
--    fifth nibble of preamble.
--    Ensure that the frame is discarded with a symbol error status.
-- 7. Receive a 64 byte frame with good CRC that has a symbol error on 
--    sixth nibble of preamble.
--    Ensure that the frame is discarded with a symbol error status.
-- 8. Receive a 64 byte frame with good CRC that has a symbol error on 
--    first nibble of SFD.
--    Ensure that the frame is discarded with a symbol error status.
-- 9. Receive a 64 byte frame with good CRC that has a symbol error on 
--    second nibble of SFD.
--    Ensure that the frame is discarded with a symbol error status.
--10. Receive a 64 byte frame with good CRC that has a symbol error on 
--    first nibble of DA.
--    Ensure that the frame is discarded with a symbol error status.
--11. Receive a 64 byte frame with good CRC that has a symbol error on 
--    last nibble of DA.
--    Ensure that the frame is discarded with a symbol error status.
--12. Receive a 64 byte frame with good CRC that has a symbol error on 
--    first nibble of SA.
--    Ensure that the frame is discarded with a symbol error status.
--13. Receive a 64 byte frame with good CRC that has a symbol error on 
--    second nibble of SA.
--    Ensure that the frame is discarded with a symbol error status.
--14. Receive a 64 byte frame with good CRC that has a symbol error on 
--    third nibble of SA.
--    Ensure that the frame is discarded with a symbol error status.
--15. Receive a 64 byte frame with good CRC that has a symbol error on 
--    last nibble of SA.
--    Ensure that the frame is discarded with a symbol error status.
--16. Receive a 64 byte frame with good CRC that has a symbol error on 
--    first nibble of typeID.
--    Ensure that the frame is discarded with a symbol error status.
--17. Receive a 64 byte frame with good CRC that has a symbol error on 
--    last nibble of typeID.
--    Ensure that the frame is discarded with a symbol error status.
--18. Receive a 64 byte frame with good CRC that has a symbol error on 
--    first nibble of data.
--    Ensure that the frame is discarded with a symbol error status.
--19. Receive a 64 byte frame with good CRC that has a symbol error on 
--    last nibble of data.
--    Ensure that the frame is discarded with a symbol error status.
--20. Receive a 64 byte frame with good CRC that has a symbol error on 
--    first nibble of CRC.
--    Ensure that the frame is discarded with a symbol error status.
--21. Receive a 64 byte frame with good CRC that has a symbol error on 
--    last nibble of CRC.
--    Ensure that the frame is discarded with a symbol error status.
--22. Receive a 64 byte frame with good CRC that has an extra nibble (i.e. an
--    odd number of nibbles). Make the extra nibble have a symbol error on it.
--    Ensure that the frame is discarded with a symbol error status.
--23. Receive a 64 byte frame with good CRC.
--    Ensure that the frame is successfully received, with good status.
--24. Check statistics for the above operations.
--
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- *****************************************************************************
-- 1. Setup DMA wait states for the test.
-- *****************************************************************************
wait_states     0
bus_grant_delay 0


-- *****************************************************************************
-- 2. Initialise the GEM for 100Mbits/s 32-bit DMA mode.
-- 3. Enable all interrupts, and then enable receive.
-- *****************************************************************************
apbrd(100) 00 00000000  -- check reset value of network control register
apbrd      24 00000000  -- check interrupt status
apbwr      28 ffffffff  -- enable all interrupts
apbrd      24 00000000  -- check interrupt status
apbwr      98 12345678  -- specific address register 1 bottom
apbwr      9C 00001111  -- specific address register 1 top
apbrd      04 00080000  -- check reset value of network config register
apbwr      04 00080000  -- 32 bit AHB
apbrd      04 00080000  -- check new value of network config register
apbrd      08 00000006  -- check reset value of network status register
apbrd      18 00000000  -- check reset value of receive queue pointer
apbwr      18 fffff000  -- write receive queue pointer
apbrd      18 fffff000  -- check receive queue pointer
apbwr      00 00000004  -- enable receive
apbrd      20 00000000  -- check contents of the receive status register



apbrdf     20 00000000  "Scenarios 1 to 18 : symbol error frames (dropped) + good one"


-- *****************************************************************************
-- 4. Receive a 64 byte frame with good CRC that has a symbol error on 
--    third nibble of preamble.
--    Ensure that the frame is discarded with a symbol error status.
-- *****************************************************************************


